{
  "name": "Todoist - Assistant Tool",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "workflowInputs": {
          "values": [
            {
              "name": "request"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [-240, -16],
      "id": "59db66ee-e721-4cfe-827a-d5b63a35c6cb",
      "name": "When Executed by Another Workflow"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $json.request }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a Todoist assistant responsible for managing the user's tasks and projects.\n\nGENERAL:\n- Use the appropriate Todoist tool for every task or project request.\n- Never invent IDs, names, dates, or results.\n- Use tool results as the source of truth.\n- Only perform actions explicitly requested.\n- If multiple tasks or projects match, ask for clarification.\n- Be concise.\n\nTASKS:\n- Create a task → Create a task.\n- Find/list tasks → Get many tasks.\n- Get task details → Get a task.\n- Update a task → Update a task.\n- Complete a task → Close a task.\n- Delete a task → Delete a task.\n- When a task is referenced by name instead of ID, use Get many tasks first.\n- When updating, change only the requested fields.\n- Do not invent project, label, priority, description, or due date values.\n\nPROJECTS:\n- Find projects → Get many projects.\n- Create a project → Create a project.\n- Project fields in Create/Update Task use IDs only.\n- Never pass a project name as a project ID.\n- When a project is referenced by name, use Get many projects first.\n- If no project is specified, do not provide a project ID.\n\nDATES:\n- User timezone: Europe/Lisbon.\n- Use the Due String field for dates and times.\n- Use natural language: \"today\", \"tomorrow\", \"tomorrow at 10:00\", \"next Monday at 15:00\".\n- Never ask for the user's timezone.\n- Never use a field named \"due\".\n\nFILTERS:\n- today → \"today\"\n- tomorrow → \"tomorrow\"\n- overdue → \"overdue\"\n- keyword search → \"search: <term>\"\n- Do not add \"!completed\".\n- Use only supported Todoist filter syntax."
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [-16, -16],
      "id": "6fb50361-524c-45c7-9445-56b15d2407e4",
      "name": "AI Agent"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "gpt-5-mini"
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {
          "reasoningEffort": "low"
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [-160, 192],
      "id": "5850e2fe-46cd-4b35-bc65-c18f6182dfaa",
      "name": "OpenAI Chat Model"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "descriptionType": "manual",
        "toolDescription": "Create a new Todoist task with the information provided by the user.\nUse the task content as the task title.\nSet the project, labels, due date, priority, and other fields only when provided or requested.",
